      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/a51f08c4b52f4eb8993b00ef8972b6ea7313c8d4/docs%2Fdocs%2Fhardware-platforms%2Fxpu.mdx",
      "changes": 16,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fhardware-platforms%2Fxpu.mdx?ref=a51f08c4b52f4eb8993b00ef8972b6ea7313c8d4",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/docs/hardware-platforms/xpu.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -50,6 +50,19 @@ cp pyproject_xpu.toml pyproject.toml\n # Install SGLang dependent libs, and build SGLang main package\n pip install --upgrade pip setuptools\n pip install -v \".[dev,diffusion]\" --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/xpu\n+\n+# Needed for XPU graph with --tp > 1; pip's warning about torch's pins is expected\n+pip install \\\n+      \"intel-cmplr-lib-rt==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-cmplr-lib-ur==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-cmplr-lic-rt==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-sycl-rt==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"oneccl-devel==2022.1.2; platform_system == 'Linux' and platform_machine == 'x86_64'\" \\\n+      \"oneccl==2022.1.2; platform_system == 'Linux' and platform_machine == 'x86_64'\" \\\n+      \"dpcpp-cpp-rt==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-opencl-rt==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-openmp==2026.1.1\" \\\n+      \"intel-pti==1.1.0\"\n ```\n \n ### Install Using Docker\n@@ -179,6 +192,9 @@ SGLang enables XPU graph capture to reduce per-step kernel-launch overhead.\n | Decode | `full` | One `torch.xpu.XPUGraph` per batch size, captured on startup | **Off** (opt-in) |\n | Prefill | `breakable` | Segmented `torch.xpu.XPUGraph` capture/replay (no `torch.compile`); eager break points at attention / MoE boundaries | **Off** (opt-in) |\n \n+> **Note:** XPU graphs with `--tp` > 1 require oneAPI 2026.1.1, oneCCL 2022.1.2 and PTI 1.1.0. The Docker image\n+> includes them; for a source install, see [Install From Source](#install-from-source).\n+\n ### Enable Decode Graph\n \n Decode graph capture is **opt-in** on XPU. Enable it explicitly:",
